      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sin\\left(56^\\circ\\right)}{\\cos^2\\left(28^\\circ\\right)}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write $s=\\sin\\left(28^\\circ\\right)$ and $c=\\cos\\left(28^\\circ\\right)$. The **double-angle formula** gives $\\sin\\left(56^\\circ\\right)=2sc$.\n\n\n\nCancel one factor of the squared denominator, then rewrite the quotient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2sc}{c^2} &=\\frac{2s}{c} \\\\ &=2\\tan\\left(28^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll cancellations use nonzero factors in the original expression.",
